        <!-- Section 10: HRX Native Execution -->
        <section id="hrx" class="space-y-4 border-b border-[#3e4042]/50 pb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">HRX Native Execution (.#hrx)</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            The <code class="text-[#25c2a0] font-mono">.#hrx</code> Nix package contains both the normal HIP route through HRX's compatibility layer and the direct native HRX/Loom executor selected with <code class="text-[#25c2a0] font-mono">--qwen-backend hrx-native</code>.
          </p>

          <div class="docusaurus-code">
            <div class="docusaurus-code-header">
              <span>Building and Benchmarking with HRX</span>
              <span>sh</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-200 space-y-2">
              <div><span class="text-slate-500"># 1. Build the HRX release package</span></div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">nix build .#hrx</div>
              <div class="text-slate-500 pt-2"># 2. Run benchmark with native HRX route</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">./result/bin/gufo bench --model models/Qwen3.8-27B-Q8_0.gguf --qwen-backend hrx-native --n-gen 8 --repetitions 3</div>
              <div class="text-slate-500 pt-2"># 3. Validate correctness against independent HIP reference</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">./result/bin/gufo bench --model models/Qwen3.8-27B-Q8_0.gguf --qwen-backend hrx-native --validate-hrx 1</div>
              <div class="text-slate-500 pt-2"># 4. Synchronized stage trace (embedding, attention, SSM, FFN, final-head)</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">GUFO_HRX_TRACE_STAGES=1 ./result/bin/gufo bench --model models/Qwen3.8-27B-Q8_0.gguf --qwen-backend hrx-native</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 11: OCI Images -->
        <section id="toolboxes" class="space-y-4 border-b border-[#3e4042]/50 pb-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">OCI Images (Docker / Podman)</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            The companion <a href="https://github.com/gufo-org/toolboxes" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-[#25c2a0] font-bold hover:underline">gufo-org/toolboxes</a> repository publishes reproducible Nix-built images for Docker and Podman. Toolbx and Distrobox are intentionally unsupported, which keeps the images free of sudo, PAM, and user-injection scaffolding.
          </p>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[#242526] border border-[#3e4042] space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-xs font-mono uppercase">gufo-runtime</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
                Inference &amp; serving image with minimal footprint, ROCm 6.3 <code class="text-slate-300">gfx1151</code> and XRT drivers.
              </p>
              <div class="bg-[#1b1b1d] p-2 rounded text-[11px] font-mono text-emerald-400">
                ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/gufo-runtime:latest
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[#242526] border border-[#3e4042] space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-xs font-mono uppercase">gufo-dev</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
                Complete interactive kernel development SDK with `hipcc`, `rocprofv3`, LLVM, CMake, Ninja, and ablation harnesses.
              </p>
              <div class="bg-[#1b1b1d] p-2 rounded text-[11px] font-mono text-cyan-400">
                ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/gufo-dev:latest
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[#242526] border border-[#3e4042] space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-xs font-mono uppercase">eval-agent</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
                Reproducible coding-agent evaluator for an OpenAI-compatible endpoint you select with <code class="text-slate-300">--base-url</code>.
              </p>
              <div class="bg-[#1b1b1d] p-2 rounded text-[11px] font-mono text-violet-400">
                ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/eval-agent:latest
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="p-4 rounded-lg bg-[#242526] border border-[#3e4042] space-y-2">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-white text-xs font-mono uppercase">gufo-eval-agent</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
                Gufo and eval-agent together. Its launcher starts a local server, waits for readiness, runs the evaluation, and stops the server.
              </p>
              <div class="bg-[#1b1b1d] p-2 rounded text-[11px] font-mono text-amber-400">
                ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/gufo-eval-agent:latest
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="admonition admonition-tip">
            <div class="admonition-title">
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
              </svg>
              <span>Dedicated non-root user</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              Containers run as <code class="text-[#25c2a0] font-mono">gufo</code> (UID/GID 1000:1000), not root. Rootless Podman maps the caller to that account with <code class="text-slate-200">--userns=keep-id:uid=1000,gid=1000</code>; <code class="text-slate-200">--group-add keep-groups</code> preserves GPU group access with the crun runtime. Docker users instead pass the numeric GPU GIDs and make writable mounts accessible to UID 1000. Evaluation runs add <code class="text-slate-200">seccomp=unconfined</code> so Bubblewrap can create its nested sandbox.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="docusaurus-code">
            <div class="docusaurus-code-header">
              <span>Run Gufo with GPU access</span>
              <span>sh</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-200 space-y-2">
              <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">podman run --rm -it --userns=keep-id:uid=1000,gid=1000 \\</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;--device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --group-add keep-groups \\</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;--ulimit memlock=-1 ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/gufo-runtime:latest gufo diagnose</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="docusaurus-code">
              <div class="docusaurus-code-header">
                <span>Evaluate your endpoint</span>
                <span>sh</span>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-200 space-y-2">
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">podman run --rm -it --userns=keep-id:uid=1000,gid=1000 \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;--network host \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;--security-opt seccomp=unconfined \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/eval-agent:latest \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;eval-agent run sparql-university --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1</div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="docusaurus-code">
              <div class="docusaurus-code-header">
                <span>Serve locally, then evaluate</span>
                <span>sh</span>
              </div>
              <div class="p-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-200 space-y-2">
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">podman run --rm -it --userns=keep-id:uid=1000,gid=1000 \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;--device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --group-add keep-groups \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;--ulimit memlock=-1 --security-opt seccomp=unconfined \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;-v /models:/models:ro \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;ghcr.io/gufo-org/toolboxes/gufo-eval-agent:latest \\</div>
                <div class="text-emerald-400 break-all">&nbsp;&nbsp;eval-agent-with-gufo --model /models/model.gguf -- run sparql-university</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 12: Systemd Service Integration -->
        <section id="systemd" class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">Systemd Background Serving</h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Run <code class="text-[#25c2a0] font-mono">gufo serve</code> as a background systemd user service for automatic startup and persistent local inference endpoints:
          </p>

          <div class="docusaurus-code">
            <div class="docusaurus-code-header">
              <span>Systemd User Service Setup</span>
              <span>sh</span>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-200 space-y-2">
              <div><span class="text-slate-500"># Enable and start user service</span></div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">cp systemd/gufo-serve.service ~/.config/systemd/user/</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">systemctl --user daemon-reload</div>
              <div class="text-emerald-400">systemctl --user enable --now gufo-serve</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>
